/* book Worked example: Q: A balanced star-connected load of Z = 10 + j6 Ω per phase is connected to a 400 V, 50 Hz three-phase supply. Find the phase current, line current, total real power and neutral current.
   1. Line voltage VL = 400 V. For star, Vph = VL/√3 = 400/1.732 = 230.9 V.
   2. |Z| = √(10² + 6²) = √136 = 11.66 Ω. φ = tan⁻¹(6/10) = 31.0°. cos φ = 10/11.66 = 0.857 lagging.
   3. Iph = Vph/|Z| = 230.9/11.66 = 19.8 A.
   4. In star, line current IL = Iph = 19.8 A.
   5. Total real power: P = 3 Iph² R = 3 × 19.8² × 10 = 11.76 kW. Check: √3 VL IL cos φ = 1.732 × 400 × 19.8 × 0.857 = 11.76 kW.
   6. The three currents are equal and 120° apart. Their phasor sum is zero, so neutral current IN = 0 A.
   Answer: Iph = IL = 19.8 A, total real power P = 11.76 kW, neutral current IN = 0 A. */
